    "final_text": "I've added the v2.4.0 release notes (dated 2026-10-20) to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, under the file's title:\n\n```\n## v2.4.0 (2026-10-20)\n\n### Breaking changes\n- None.\n\n### Features\n- You can now export reports to CSV from the `report` command. [ACME-412] (thanks @mira)\n- Uploads now retry automatically with backoff when the server is temporarily unavailable (HTTP 503). [ACME-415] (thanks @jonas)\n\n### Fixes\n- Acme no longer crashes when the config file is empty. [ACME-419] (thanks @tom)\n- Monthly summaries now show correct totals in leap years. [ACME-423] (thanks @priya)\n```\n\nACME-421 is left out as you asked. It was the only breaking change (it removed the `--legacy` flag from sync), so \"Breaking changes\" now says \"None.\" The house format keeps that section even when it's empty. I didn't touch the older v2.3.0 and v2.2.0 entries.",
